Package: lowrankbandit
Type: Package
Title: Greedy Low-Rank Contextual GLM Bandits and Two-Track Inference
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ke", "Xu", email = "kxu6@nd.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Yuefeng", "Han", role = "aut"),
    person("Zifeng", "Zhao", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Contextual bandits whose rewards follow a generalized linear model with a
    low-rank interaction between the features of the arms and the context. The greedy policy
    learns the interaction by nuclear-norm-penalized estimation, refitted every round after a
    short exploration (Algorithm 1). Two-track cross-fitting then gives confidence intervals
    for linear functionals of the parameter that are asymptotically valid although the data were
    collected by greedy, non-randomized choices (Algorithm 2). The functions, arguments and
    defaults are those of the Python package of the same name, which returns the same numbers on
    the same rounds.
